---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
const title = 'Responsible Disclosure Policy'
const description = 'How to report a security vulnerability in Grassion.'
---

<Base {title} {description}>
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 text-gray-200">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Responsible Disclosure Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-10">Last updated: 2026-11-05</p>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">Our commitment</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
        Grassion takes the security of our systems and our customers' data seriously. If you have
        discovered a security vulnerability, we appreciate your help in disclosing it to us in a
        responsible manner.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">How to report</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Email your findings to
        <a href="mailto:security@grassion.com" class="text-green-400 hover:underline">
          security@grassion.com
        </a>.
        Please include:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-400 space-y-1 ml-2">
        <li>A description of the vulnerability and its potential impact</li>
        <li>Steps to reproduce (proof-of-concept or screenshots if available)</li>
        <li>Any relevant URLs or affected components</li>
        <li>Your contact details (optional — we can respond anonymously)</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mt-4">
        If you believe the report is sensitive, please encrypt it with our PGP key (available on
        request).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">What to expect</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-400 space-y-2 ml-2">
        <li>Acknowledgement of your report within <strong class="text-white">2 business days</strong>.</li>
        <li>An initial assessment and severity classification within <strong class="text-white">5 business days</strong>.</li>
        <li>Regular status updates while we work on a fix.</li>
        <li>Credit in the fix announcement (if you would like it).</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">Scope</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-3">In scope:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-400 space-y-1 ml-2 mb-4">
        <li>api.grassion.com</li>
        <li>app.grassion.com</li>
        <li>grassion.com</li>
        <li>The Grassion GitHub App</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-3">Out of scope:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-400 space-y-1 ml-2">
        <li>Denial-of-service attacks</li>
        <li>Social engineering of Grassion employees</li>
        <li>Physical security</li>
        <li>Vulnerabilities in third-party services we depend on (report those upstream)</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">Safe harbour</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
        We will not take legal action against researchers who act in good faith under this policy,
        provided they avoid accessing data beyond what is needed to demonstrate the vulnerability,
        do not degrade our service, and report to us without disclosing the issue publicly until a
        fix is in place.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">PGP key</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
        A PGP public key for <code class="text-green-400">security@grassion.com</code> is available
        on request. Email us and we will reply with the key.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
